      "body": "Function parameter and return annotations are evaluated in the surrounding scope on supported Python versions, but the process-group checker skips them when overriding the function visitor. Inspect those expressions before entering the function body scope.\n\nValidation: four annotation forms fail baseline detection and pass with the fix. The 29 existing stdlib checker tests also pass. CPU-only checker validation; no GPU run.\n\nFollow-up review validation: Postponed annotations are excluded while defaults and decorators remain checked. Three focused methods and all 29 existing checker tests pass.\n\nReview requested: @NVIDIA/mcore-oncall. This PR is ready for review with CPU regression evidence above. Upstream runner validation remains subject to NVIDIA contributor vetting.\n",
